    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d96">

                <pb facs="0111" n="99" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg99"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.01/530: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Prime Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Churchill</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to President Roosevelt </hi><anchor
                        n="37" xml:id="d96-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-04-18">April 18, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>651. Your 523. Thank you so much. I have told our people to make use of your
                    message to the King and his new Ministers and to read it to mutinous brigade and
                    recalcitrant ships. It may have a most salutary effect. I am not publishing
                    anything here.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d96-f1" n="37" type="source" xml:id="d96-f1-content">
                <p>Copy forwarded to the Secretary of State by the British Ambassador (Halifax) on
                    April 19.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
